+#### Retries
+
+The `retry` field of an `HTTPRoute` rule retries the request to the backend, as defined by [GEP-1731](https://gateway-api.sigs.k8s.io/geps/gep-1731/).
+Traefik adds a [Retry](../http/middlewares/retry.md) middleware to the routers of the rule, after the middlewares of the route-level filters, so that only the call to the backend is retried.
+
+| Field | Behavior |
+| --- | --- |
+| `attempts` | Number of retries after the first request. Defaults to `1`. |
+| `codes` | Response status codes that trigger a retry. Traefik also retries on connection errors. |
+| `backoff` | Wait time before the first retry. Later waits grow up to twice this value. |
+
+Traefik does not retry `POST`, `PATCH`, and `LOCK` requests, because they are not idempotent.
+
+Traefik buffers the request body to send it again.
+A request with a body larger than [`retryMaxRequestBodyBytes`](../../install-configuration/providers/kubernetes/kubernetes-gateway.md#opt-providers-kubernetesGateway-retryMaxRequestBodyBytes) (2 MB by default) is forwarded without retry.
+
+```yaml tab="HTTPRoute"
+---
+apiVersion: gateway.networking.k8s.io/v1
+kind: HTTPRoute
+metadata:
+  name: whoami-http
+  namespace: default
+spec:
+  parentRefs:
+    - name: traefik
+      sectionName: http
+      kind: Gateway
+
+  hostnames:
+    - whoami.localhost
+
+  rules:
+    - backendRefs:
+        - name: whoami
+          namespace: default
+          port: 80
+      retry:
+        attempts: 3
+        codes:
+          - 502
+          - 503
+        backoff: 100ms
+```
+
 ### GRPC
 
 The `GRPCRoute` is an extended resource in the Gateway API specification, designed to define how GRPC traffic should be routed within a Kubernetes cluster. 
